piano or violin.assistantfinalThe problem is that the input text is not a well‑formed LaTeX document.  The compiler is trying to parse a fragment that contains a lot of stray text, a `\begin{document}` that is never closed, a `\begin{align}` that is never closed, and a huge block of plain text that is not valid LaTeX.  Because of that, the compiler keeps looking for the matching `\end{align}` and `\end{document}` and eventually runs out of input, producing the “Run‑time error: TeX capacity exceeded” message.

To fix it you need to turn the snippet into a valid LaTeX file.  For example:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\begin{document}

\begin{align}
\text{(your equations here)}
\end{align}

% If you want to include the long block of text, put it in a
% \begin{verbatim}…\end{verbatim} or \begin{quote}…\end{quote} block, or
% simply write it as normal paragraph text.

\end{document}
```

